<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine rains helping maize - government.</title>
<headline>Argentine rains helping maize - government.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Recent rains provided excellent conditions for the development of Argentina's maize crop, Agriculture Secretariat said in its Jan 17 weekly crop report released Thursday.</p>
<p>Maize plants now flowering are benefitting especially. But there is concern over the appearance of Rio Cuarto disease in many maize zones, and the degree of the problem is being evaluated. Farmers had sown 98.1 percent of their maize by Jan 17, as well as 99.0 percent of their soybeans and 99.4 percent of their sunflowers. They had harvested 99.7 percent of their 1996/97 wheat crop.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets).</p>
